module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_arm_degraded_between_converges_with_nothing_observing

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_arm_degraded_between_converges_with_nothing_observing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_arm_degraded_between_converges_with_nothing_observing" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "AN ARM WAS DEGRADED FOR ALMOST FOUR HOURS AND NOTHING NOTICED. The arm converge (docs/plans/arm-convergence-recovery-design.md) observes the arm only when a converge runs. Between converges nothing reads it, so a rank that dies is first seen by the NEXT converge -- or by a person -- and the arm reports nothing in the meantime.",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-10-05, Group A fp8-16: the arm was started by hand at 03:45Z and adopted as committed by converge run 37275627394. Its units are bounded experiments (gunbc.spark.native_serving_realization arm_unit_lifetime_for, ArmBoundedExperiment: RuntimeMaxSec 4h 39min 36s, derived by arm_memory_experiment_runtime). srv5's rank reached its runtime limit at 08:19Z ('Failed with result timeout'), so from 08:19Z the arm could not serve, and it stayed that way until converge run 37304585650 observed the dead rank at 12:04Z and restarted the whole arm. The whole-arm Apply was the correct remedy; the defect is the four hours before it.",

    "TWO FACTS ARE MISSING, AND THEY ARE SEPARATE. (1) No observer of the arm between converges: the converge's own observation (gunbc.spark.arm_convergence arm_rank_observe, typed legs, plus the readback) is the right read, but nothing runs it on a schedule, and no consumer is told when it would diverge. (2) The bounded experiment's expiry is a KNOWN, scheduled end -- the unit's RuntimeMaxSec fixes it at start -- yet it surfaces as an unexplained dead rank. An arm parked between staircase steps under an experiment intent therefore always ends this way, about 4h40m after each start, and the end looks like a crash.",

    "OPERATOR RULINGS, 2026-10-06 (relayed by valiant-crab-775). (1) Between staircase steps Group A stays a BOUNDED EXPERIMENT: RuntimeMaxSec is kept, no standing-serve intent is added, and each step re-converges; persistent serving comes only through ArmNormalServing (an established fit plus promotion receipts). (2) NO scheduled observe: no cadence or schedule trigger for spark_arm_group_observe. An unobserved degraded arm is ACCEPTED between converges for a bounded experiment, and it is surfaced at the next converge, which observes first.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder for four hours (silent degradation), caught by the next converge. RUNG NOW: an accepted, bounded residue for a bounded experiment, per ruling (2) -- the degradation is surfaced, at the latest, by the next converge's own observation, and a converge never acts on an arm it has not observed. The scheduled end is no longer discovered: the commit records each rank's expiry instant (gunbc.spark.native_serving_apply spark_native_commit_record_script writes expires=<ActiveEnterTimestamp + RuntimeMaxSec>; gunbc.spark.arm_convergence arm_committed_expiry_of reads it), and a converge past it reports the arm ENDED AS SCHEDULED rather than as unexplained dead ranks. CEILING: as ruled -- an unobserved window is accepted for a bounded experiment and does not climb further. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an arm promoted to ArmNormalServing, whose persistent units have no scheduled end; a persistent arm degrading unobserved is NOT covered by this acceptance and reopens this row.",

  ],

  evidence: [],
}
